"""TagConnect TC2030-IDC-NL 6-pad land pattern wired as 4-wire JTAG.

The 6-pad Tag-Connect TC2030 carries a target-voltage reference, a ground
reference, and four signal pads. That fits a complete 4-wire JTAG bus
(TMS, TCK, TDI, TDO) but leaves no room for nRESET — the target board
must reset the device through another path (e.g. an EN/nRST button) and
the probe drives only the JTAG state machine.

Pad layout (matches the Tag-Connect TC2030 numbering used by KiCad's
`Tag-Connect_TC2030-IDC-NL_2x03_P1.27mm_Vertical` footprint, which is the
same physical pad map as the ARM SWD variant — only the signal assignment
to pads 2/3/4/6 is repurposed for JTAG):

    1  VTref      (target-voltage reference)
    2  TMS
    3  TCK
    4  TDI
    5  GND
    6  TDO

No part is populated; the TC2030-IDC-NL cable mates directly to the pads.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Jtag")

VTREF = io(Power(voltage="1.2V to 5.5V"))
GND = io(Ground)
JTAG = io(Jtag)

Component(
    name="J",
    symbol=Symbol(library="TagConnect.kicad_sym", name="TC2030"),
    pins={
        "1": VTREF,
        "2": JTAG.TMS,
        "3": JTAG.TCK,
        "4": JTAG.TDI,
        "5": GND,
        "6": JTAG.TDO,
    },
    skip_bom=True,
    skip_pos=True,
)
